# Applies to every image built with the REPO ROOT as context
# (Dockerfile.observer-org, Dockerfile.observer-mcpgw, Dockerfile.observer-cloud,
# deploy/observer-{devnode,node,edge,gateway}/Dockerfile). Those are all
# pure-Go builds; every go:embed asset lives under internal/ (the dashboards
# embed internal/*/webapp/dist, not web//web2/ directly), so the web sources,
# distribution channels, and the private marketing/site trees are dead weight
# in the build context (~20 GB without this file).
# harness-gateway builds from its OWN directory context and is unaffected.
#
# RULE (tests/invariant/dockerignore_test.go pins it): every `!` exception in
# this file is a plain path, never a wildcard (* ? [ ]). One wildcard
# exception makes BuildKit walk INTO every excluded directory looking for
# re-included files, so an excluded directory the builder cannot read (the
# demo box's state/router/caddy, root 0700 once Caddy has run in direct
# public mode) still fails the build with "permission denied". Exclusions
# may use wildcards freely.

.git
.wrangler
bin
tmp
marketing
harness-gateway
model-pricing
website
design
web
# web/package.json stays: the npm workspace root lists web/ as a member, and
# `npm ci` in Dockerfile.observer-org's web2 stage needs every member's
# manifest. The rest of web/ is not in the context.
!web/package.json
# web2/ IS in the context: Dockerfile.observer-org builds the org dashboard
# from source and syncs it into the embed (P3-07), so an image can never ship
# a stale committed embed. Its build output is not.
web2/dist
vscode
sdk
npm
pypi
docs
# docs/embed.go embeds the eight deployment runbooks into observer-org
# (`observer-org deploy export`); exactly those files plus the embed
# declaration are re-included, or the go:embed pattern fails the image build.
# Named one by one (see RULE above); the invariant test checks this list
# against docs/embed.go's go:embed line.
!docs/embed.go
!docs/deploy-observer-org-production.md
!docs/private-datacenter-deployment.md
!docs/teams-getting-started.md
!docs/teams-operations.md
!docs/teams-architecture.md
!docs/enterprise-updates.md
!docs/aigateway-runbook.md
!docs/harness-sdk-playbook.md
browser-extension
observer
observer.exe
*.log
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Deploy-kit runtime state and operator secrets (T-936) -------------------
# Every Dockerfile above has a `COPY . .` build stage, so anything a deploy
# kit leaves in the working tree reaches that stage and the builder's cache
# whenever an image is built from a checkout that is also a running kit (the
# demo box builds from ~/sbo-demo, which IS its kit). deploy/embed.go also
# go:embeds all:observer-org/production and all:modules, so a filled .env,
# a secrets/ directory or a local tofu state there would land IN the
# observer-org binary. Release images build from `git archive` and never
# carried any of this; working-tree builds could.
#
# Box kits' generated state: database, broker and sidecar passwords, keys,
# rendered config, Caddy's certificate store.
deploy/demo-box/state
deploy/cloud-box/state
# Operator-created secret directories the compose files bind-mount.
deploy/observer-org/production/secrets
deploy/observer-gateway/config
# Every .env and .env.* at any depth: the demo box's .env, keygen.sh's
# deploy/observer-org/.env, a filled production or observer-mcpgw .env.
# The OpenTofu test-bundle .env fixtures under deploy/modules/**/tests/ go
# too; `observer-org deploy export` never ships tests/ (deploybundle prunes it).
**/.env
**/.env.*
# The one template a build needs: observer-org go:embeds it for
# `observer-org deploy export`.
!deploy/observer-org/production/.env.example
# Local OpenTofu state, its provider cache and filled tfvars. The committed
# tfvars fixtures live deeper (tests/fixtures/) and stay.
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.terraform
deploy/modules/*/*/*/*.tfvars
deploy/modules/*/*/*/*.tfvars.json
deploy/ops/**/*.tfvars
